  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Salis beach is a long sandy beach at the foot of Cap d'Antibes, shallow and close to old Antibes. The tourist office describes it with lifeguard posts, toilets and showers, and a Handi-plage point near the water sports centre.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>No official source says dogs are allowed on this beach. The Handiplage page for La Salis, published by the Antibes Juan-les-Pins tourist office (updated March 2026), states that "dogs are not allowed on the beaches or in the water", except guide dogs for the blind and assistance dogs (on presentation of the official document and vest). The tourist office page gives no dates and the municipal order is not published online: call the town hall before coming with your dog, especially in summer, when the beach is busiest. The regional tourism listing for the beach also shows a generic "animals accepted" icon, which the tourist office's Handiplage page clearly contradicts for the beaches and the water.</p>
      <p>The tourist office presents the beach as one of the two long sandy beaches (with Ponteil) on leaving old Antibes, shallow, with a large car park, a sailing school and a Handi-plage point. It specifies that guide dogs for the blind and assistance dogs are admitted on presentation of the official document and vest.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if in doubt, favour the Cap d'Antibes coastal path, a stone's throw away, for a walk with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The beach lies on the way out of old Antibes towards Cap d'Antibes, which the coastal path follows.</p>
